accounting: "THE EPIC'S HAND-OFF, END TO END. design-scope lists three artifacts at this tip, the component designs W12 and W13 wrote and retired inside their WUs at bytes main never held (DEC-29); each is cited at its last state, the blob its WU cited: help.html at 4f3a3c4c (802ddfe5, W13), menu-path.html and step-media.html at 4367f999 (957e4e2a and fb4ff0d9, W12). Their designs now live in the TSDoc of Help, MenuPath and StepMedia (DEC-16). The two design runs leave the tree at adfcb739 and are cited at their last state reachable from the tip (DEC-28), each data-status archived there: the setup screen's run at a2a9395b (round 23, the last of rounds 10-23 opened and closed inside W1-W15, each judged on its own seam), and the close dialog's at 005518d0 (W11, closed on the owner's LGTM). The four new surfaces are cited: Help, MenuPath and StepMedia to their component designs, QrCode to the setup run (round 11, W2; its forks are DEC-57's). Every other rendered file is built from one of the two runs, except CommandBlock, declared above. W16-W19 changed these files without a round, by the owner's word ('I don't need the design run, just build it'), and their own notes declared each edit undesigned with its reason (copy and render conditions inside the layout of record, StepMedia's height token at W18, MenuPath's spaced arrows at W17); at the epic those files still render the layout the run closed on, so they are cited to it. The epic review's fixes (37a09ba2 to the tip) touch one rendered file, App.tsx, and only its machine read's wiring: the certificate fetch bounded, nothing rendered differently. W21, after the first close, changed seven of these files with no design run by the owner's ruling ('no need mock up just build it', 2026-11-02), and its own design/v1 note declared each edit undesigned with its reason: the ? and its open flag left Help, whose note keeps help.html's anatomy (Inter 11px ink-mute under its line) and is drawn while one switch is on (DEC-66); the